<tr style=3D"text-align:left;vertical-align:middle"><td style=3D"width:100%;=
border-collapse:collapse;color:#a8a8a8;font-family:Helvetica,Arial,sans-seri=
f;font-size:11px;font-weight:bold;line-height:1.3;margin:0;padding:0px 0px 0=
px 0px;text-align:left;vertical-align:middle;word-wrap:break-word">
            Acceptance of the baggage without complaint made before leaving t=
he transit area and without completion of the Property Irregularity Report (=
PIR) is considered to be evidence that the baggage has been delivered in goo=
d condition and in accordance with the contract of carriage. For more inform=
ation regarding baggage claim please refer to the proper section of the
            <a style=3D"color:#660f6e;font-weight:normal" href=3D"https://wi=
zzair.com/en-gb/legal/general-conditions-of-carriage-for-passengers-and-bagg=
age?utm_source=3Dwizz&amp;utm_medium=3Demail&amp;utm_campaign=3Dsystem_email=
_itinerary_confirmation&amp;utm_content=3Dclaims">general conditions of carr=
iage</a>.
            <br><br>
            Complaints relating to the carriage by air (other than baggage c=
laims) must be made in writing as soon as possible, after arrival of the fli=
ght in connection with which you would like to complain, but not later than w=
ithin 2 months from discovering the circumstances giving rise to the complai=
nt. You are liable for any loss or damage arising from the delay in making y=
our complaint. Wizz Air will assess the complaint according to the general c=
onditions of carriage effective on the day of the contract.
            <br><br>
            Please file your complaints through the following website:
            <a style=3D"color:#660f6e;font-weight:normal" href=3D"https://wi=
zzair.com/en-gb/information-and-services/compliments-and-complaints/?utm_sou=
rce=3Dwizz&amp;utm_medium=3Demail&amp;utm_campaign=3Dsystem_email_itinerary_=
confirmation">https://wizzair.com/en-gb/information-and-services/compliments=
-and-complaints/</a>.
